      "summary": "Fortified River Port. Inland river trade, iron and lumber distribution.",
      "content": "\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n  <p><strong>Geographical Type:</strong> Fortified River Port</p>\n  <p><strong>Strategic &amp; Economic Value:</strong> Inland river trade, iron and lumber distribution.</p>\n  <p><strong>Primary Encounter Hazards:</strong> River pirates, corrupt customs inspectors, mercenaries.</p>\n</div>\n<h3>Geographical Description</h3>\n<p>Attributes: Fortified inland river port, lower Thunder River, timber and iron hub.</p>\n<p>Guarralid</p>\n<p>Attributes: Autonomous mountain fiefdom, mineral wealth, private armies.</p>\n<p>Description: A powerful, fiercely independent interior duchy located in the highlands. Governed by proud Grandees who hoard private mineral wealth, Guarralid maintains an independent standing army and is plagued by bloody, hereditary border feuds with neighboring provinces.</p>\n\n<div class=\"gm-callout\">\n  <div class=\"gm-badge\">GM CONFIDENTIAL &bull; REGIONAL HAZARDS &amp; HOOKS</div>\n  <p><strong>Encounter Threats:</strong> River pirates, corrupt customs inspectors, mercenaries.</p>\n</div>\n",
