      "summary": "Underground fanatical theocracy operating from hidden monastic cells.",
      "content": "\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n  <p><strong>Faction Classification:</strong> Underground Fanatical Theocracy</p>\n</div>\n<h3>Faction Dossier &amp; Operations</h3>\n<p>Underground fanatical theocracy operating from hidden monastic cells.</p>\n<p>Eradicate necromancy, overthrow crown, impose divine rule.</p>\n<p>Public distrust from child crucifixion; outlawed status.</p>\n<p>Zealous antagonists or uneasy allies against necromantic threats.</p>\n\n\n<h3>The Border Sanctuaries &amp; The Covenant of San Severo</h3>\n<p>While the Church operates in deep secrecy within Kordova under <a href=\"#npcs/malachai\" class=\"wiki-link\">Father Malachai</a>, and rules openly in <a href=\"#gazetteer/velasco\" class=\"wiki-link\">Velasco</a>, its most vulnerable frontier outpost is <a href=\"#gazetteer/san-severo\" class=\"wiki-link\">San Severo del Vado</a>. Here, <a href=\"#npcs/madre-soledad\" class=\"wiki-link\">Madre Soledad 'La Marcada'</a> has turned the village chapel into a sanctuary for three hundred refugee orphans. The armed uprising of <a href=\"#factions/hermandad-de-las-espinas\" class=\"wiki-link\">La Hermandad de las Espinas</a> represents the living intersection of peasant desperation and Gnostic martyrdom, serving as the frontline buffer between the holy revolution in the south and the warlords of the capital.</p>\n",
