      "summary": "A neighboring Hyborian nation (Argos) threatens immediate war unless the signet ring of their ambassador—murdered during Mad King Daedalus's...",
      "content": "\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n  <p><strong>Involved Factions:</strong> The Triumvirate, Restoration Council, Kingdom of Argos, The Pit Underworld</p>\n  <p><strong>Strategic Reward:</strong> Prevents an immediate Argossean naval blockade of Kordava harbor, secures a foreign diplomatic reprieve, and provides potential access to the Obsidian Blade.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>Narrative Premise</h3>\n<p>A neighboring Hyborian nation (Argos) threatens immediate war unless the signet ring of their ambassador—murdered during Mad King Daedalus's ritual in Period V—is returned from an earthquake-exposed crypt beneath Kordava. The Restoration Council forbids the Triumvirate from intervening, hoping the diplomatic crisis will humiliate the crown.</p>\n\n<h3>Core Conflict &amp; Player Choice</h3>\n<p>Deep in the crypt, the PCs discover the ambassador is now a conscious, memory-retaining zombie thrall who guards the Obsidian Blade. The rulers must choose whether to destroy the thrall and return the signet ring to prevent war, free the thrall using a dangerous unbinding rite, or secretly claim the Obsidian Blade for themselves.</p>\n\n<div class=\"dc-box\">\n  <strong>Basic D&D Challenge Checks:</strong> Intelligence check to identify unbinding runes; Charisma check to appeal to living memories..\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"escalation\"><strong>Dynamic Escalation Trigger:</strong> If the PCs take longer than 3 rounds negotiating or searching the crypt, a covert strike team loyal to the Restoration Council enters from upper tunnels, ordered to seize all relics and eliminate witnesses.</p>\n",
      "gmSecrets": "Resolution of this hook permanently shifts the Crown Sovereignty clock by +1 or -1.",
