      "content": "\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n  <p><strong>Involved Factions:</strong> Restoration Council, The Triumvirate, Marquis Mateo</p>\n  <p><strong>Strategic Reward:</strong> Exposes Council embezzlement and forces release of crown funds for an independent royal guard.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>Narrative Premise</h3>\n<p>When the Triumvirate attempts to allocate funds for independent city watch recruitment, Marquis Mateo calmly informs them that crown coffers are completely dry, citing foreign debt payments owed to Argos.</p>\n\n<h3>Core Conflict &amp; Player Choice</h3>\n<p>The PCs must find a way to finance their rule without Council permission: raid an illicit black-market smuggling den in The Pit, audit Mateo's private provincial tax records, or negotiate a risky loan with foreign merchants.</p>\n\n<div class=\"dc-box\">\n  <strong>Basic D&D Challenge Checks:</strong> Intelligence check to audit treasury scrolls; Charisma check to confront Marquis Mateo..\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"escalation\"><strong>Dynamic Escalation Trigger:</strong> If confronted directly without unassailable proof, Mateo retaliates by cutting the royal palace's servant and food budgets, claiming 'extreme wartime austerity.'</p>\n",
