      "content": "\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n  <p><strong>Involved Factions:</strong> Grandee Coalitions, Restoration Council, Barachan Pirates</p>\n  <p><strong>Strategic Reward:</strong> Re-establishes crown trade tariffs along the lower Thunder River, generating independent income that frees the Triumvirate from the Council's financial leash.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>Narrative Premise</h3>\n<p>Duke Gonzalo orders his private garrison in Jerida to seize royal barges carrying timber and ore along the Thunder River, declaring an embargo until the crown cuts provincial customs tariffs.</p>\n\n<h3>Core Conflict &amp; Player Choice</h3>\n<p>The PCs must travel to Jerida to break the standoff through military intimidation, clever economic compromise, or covert sabotage of Gonzalo's supply lines.</p>\n\n<div class=\"dc-box\">\n  <strong>Basic D&D Challenge Checks:</strong> Charisma check (or 2d6 Reaction Roll) to rally merchants; Dexterity / Move Silently check to run the river blockade..\n</div>\n\n<p class=\"escalation\"><strong>Dynamic Escalation Trigger:</strong> Failure to resolve the embargo within 3 days triggers an armed clash between royal army detachments and Gonzalo's retainers, threatening full civil war.</p>\n",
