      "summary": "General Don Rodrigo de Valenza brings the PC Triumvirate to the besieged border village of San Severo del Vado, demanding they personally preside over the storming of the barricaded bridge and the summary execution of the rebel leaders. The PCs must navigate military ruthlessness, the desperate plight of religious refugees, the approaching warbands of Velasco, and their own sovereign destiny.",
      "content": "\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n  <p><strong>Involved Factions:</strong> <a href=\"#factions/military-elite\" class=\"wiki-link\">The Military Elite</a>, <a href=\"#factions/hermandad-de-las-espinas\" class=\"wiki-link\">La Hermandad de las Espinas</a>, <a href=\"#factions/church-of-nemeth\" class=\"wiki-link\">Church of Nemeth</a>, <a href=\"#gazetteer/velasco\" class=\"wiki-link\">Velasco (The Council of the Pure)</a>, The PC Triumvirate</p>\n  <p><strong>Key Locations:</strong> <em>El Puente de los Desamparados</em>, <em>La Capilla de los Afligidos</em>, The Royal Command Pavillion, <a href=\"#gazetteer/san-severo\" class=\"wiki-link\">San Severo del Vado</a></p>\n  <p><strong>Strategic Rewards:</strong> Secures vital border crossing; averts an all-out holy war with Velasco; recruits an independent veteran border guard; gains royal acclaim (+2 Crown Sovereignty); or gains supreme leverage over General Valenza.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>1. Narrative Premise &amp; Royal Dilemma</h3>\n<p>General Don Rodrigo de Valenza has marched a punitive strike force of two hundred heavy cavalry, armored pikemen, and crossbowmen to the border crossing of <a href=\"#gazetteer/san-severo\" class=\"wiki-link\">San Severo del Vado</a>. The village has barricaded the basalt bridge of <em>El Puente de los Desamparados</em>, driven out crown bailiffs, and refused to surrender winter grain or religious refugees.</p>\n\n<p>Having invited the young PC Triumvirate to accompany him to 'display royal resolution to the kingdom,' Rodrigo now places the burden directly upon their shoulders. Erecting three heavy wooden gallows on the riverbank facing the village, Rodrigo presents the young monarchs with three pre-written death warrants bearing the names of <a href=\"#npcs/andres-hojeda\" class=\"wiki-link\">Capitán Andrés de Hojeda</a>, <a href=\"#npcs/madre-soledad\" class=\"wiki-link\">Madre Soledad</a>, and <a href=\"#npcs/alcalde-cadenas\" class=\"wiki-link\">Alcalde Bartolomé Cadenas</a>.</p>\n\n<blockquote>\n  &ldquo;A king who will not spill blood to defend his law is not a sovereign, Liege—he is merely a corpse awaiting a ditch. The army watches. The Grandees watch. Sign the warrants, order the bridge stormed, and let the realm see that the crown has teeth.&rdquo;\n  <br>&mdash; <em>General Don Rodrigo de Valenza</em>\n</blockquote>\n\n<h3>2. The Three Strategic Paths &amp; Player Agency</h3>\n\n<div class=\"hook-card info-card\">\n  <h4>Path A: The Iron Hand (The Executioner's Crown)</h4>\n  <p><strong>Action:</strong> The PCs sign the decrees, sanction the military assault, and order the summary hanging of Andrés, Soledad, and Cadenas on the bridge parapets.</p>\n  <p><strong>Outcome:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>Military Acclaim:</strong> General Valenza is deeply impressed by their cold resolve (+2 Reaction Roll bonus, eliminates Command Friction in the army for 30 days). The royal army secures the border road.</li>\n    <li><strong>Catastrophic Political Fallback:</strong> The common folk and peasants of southern Zingara brand the Triumvirate as bloodthirsty butcher-puppets (-2 Crown Sovereignty).</li>\n    <li><strong>Holy Retaliation:</strong> The Council of the Pure in <a href=\"#gazetteer/velasco\" class=\"wiki-link\">Velasco</a> permanently declares the Triumvirate an 'anathema to God,' intensifying the salt and wine embargo and dispatching holy assassins to Kordova.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"hook-card info-card\">\n  <h4>Path B: The Sovereign's Prerogative (The Royal Pardon &amp; The Salt Accord)</h4>\n  <p><strong>Action:</strong> The PCs ride between the parley lines, countermand Rodrigo's assault orders under their supreme constitutional authority, and enter San Severo under royal safe-conduct to negotiate directly with the rebels.</p>\n  <p><strong>Outcome:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li><strong>The Compromise:</strong> The PCs commute the death sentences, grant a royal pardon to the deserters, convert the village into a demilitarized royal sanctuary, and grant the peasants a permanent 20% dividend on border salt gathering in exchange for reopening the road and acknowledging crown sovereignty.</li>\n    <li><strong>Recruiting the Border Guard:</strong> Capitán Andrés swears fealty directly to the Triumvirate, transforming the Brotherhood into an elite, independent frontier ranger company (<em>Los Guardas del Vado</em>) that answers solely to the monarchs, completely bypassing Valenza!</li>\n    <li><strong>Velasco Diplomatic Breakthrough:</strong> Impressed by their mercy toward the refugee orphans, Madre Soledad uses her pigeon network to open official peace talks with Velasco, offering a path to end the salt famine in Kordova.</li>\n    <li><strong>Friction with Rodrigo:</strong> Valenza is enraged by the slight to his military authority (DC 16 <a href=\"#rules/pundonor\" class=\"wiki-link\">Pundonor</a> check to soothe his aristocratic pride without provoking a duel or mutiny).</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"hook-card info-card\">\n  <h4>Path C: The Shadow Gambit (The Faked Executions &amp; The Blackmail Extraction)</h4>\n  <p><strong>Action:</strong> The PCs use stealth, necromancy, or alchemical trickery to appear to comply with Don Rodrigo while secretly spiriting Andrés and the secret documents away.</p>\n  <p><strong>Outcome:</strong></p>\n  <ul>\n    <li>Using an alchemical feign-death draught (provided by <a href=\"#npcs/escovedo\" class=\"wiki-link\">Dr. Horatio Escovedo</a>) or substituting freshly reanimated corpses disguised as the condemned, the PCs stage the hangings to satisfy Rodrigo's troops, while secretly escorting Andrés and Soledad to safety.</li>\n    <li>The PCs secure Andrés's sealed evidence proving Rodrigo's Period VII war crimes, establishing an ironclad blackmail lever over their general.</li>\n  </ul>\n</div>\n\n<h3>3. Key Challenge Checks &amp; Mechanics</h3>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>DC 15 Insight:</strong> Uncover that Don Rodrigo's urgency is driven by personal panic over Andrés's identity, not military strategy.</li>\n  <li><strong>DC 16 Warfare / Command Friction:</strong> Identify fatal flaws in Rodrigo's frontal bridge-assault plan (the hidden sulfur-pitch pots) and propose a flanking maneuver that saves soldiers' lives.</li>\n  <li><strong>DC 17 Persuasion / Pundonor:</strong> Force Rodrigo to stand down his cavalry without impugning his martial honor before his officers.</li>\n  <li><strong>DC 15 Stealth / Infiltration:</strong> Navigate the river reeds and pre-Cataclysmic drainage conduits beneath the bridge to enter San Severo undetected.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>4. Dynamic Escalation Trigger</h3>\n<p class=\"escalation\"><strong>The Horns of Velasco (The 12-Hour Clock):</strong> Madre Soledad's messenger pigeon reached Velasco. An armed river war-cog carrying eighty holy warrior-monks (<em>Los Flagelantes del Mar</em>) under Father Bartolomé the Unforgiving will arrive at the river ford in exactly 12 hours. If the bridge is still besieged or blood has been spilled when the war-cog arrives, an uncontrollable three-way battle will erupt, plunging Zingara into total civil war.</p>\n",
      "gmSecrets": "If the PCs resolve the crisis peacefully and recruit Andrés, he reveals that Rodrigo's chief cavalry captain, Capitán Fierro, is a secret member of the underground republican movement who was waiting for the right moment to defect.",
