      "summary": "Capitán Andrés de Hojeda secretly possesses the original, wax-sealed military order written by General Don Rodrigo de Valenza during the Restoration Civil War commanding the massacre of a neutral church peace delegation. If the PCs can recover this document before Rodrigo's strike teams destroy it, they gain absolute blackmail leverage to neutralize the General's coup threats.",
      "content": "\n<div class=\"info-card\">\n  <p><strong>Involved Factions:</strong> The PC Triumvirate, <a href=\"#npcs/valenza\" class=\"wiki-link\">General Don Rodrigo de Valenza</a>, <a href=\"#npcs/andres-hojeda\" class=\"wiki-link\">Capitán Andrés de Hojeda</a>, <a href=\"#factions/church-of-nemeth\" class=\"wiki-link\">Church of Nemeth</a></p>\n  <p><strong>Key Locations:</strong> The Subterranean Crypt of <em>La Capilla de los Afligidos</em>, <a href=\"#gazetteer/san-severo\" class=\"wiki-link\">San Severo del Vado</a></p>\n  <p><strong>Strategic Reward:</strong> Absolute political blackmail leverage over General Don Rodrigo de Valenza, permanently preventing him from staging a military coup or threatening the Triumvirate under Pundonor.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>1. Narrative Premise</h3>\n<p>During the parley at the bridgehead of San Severo, <a href=\"#npcs/andres-hojeda\" class=\"wiki-link\">Capitán Andrés de Hojeda</a> secretly passes a coded message or gestures toward the village chapel. If the PCs arrange a covert audience with him in the crypts of <em>La Capilla de los Afligidos</em>, Andrés reveals why Don Rodrigo is so frantic to hang him without a public trial.</p>\n\n<p>Andrés was the officer who received General Rodrigo's infamous <strong>Dispatch of the Black River</strong> during Period VII. In that sealed document, Rodrigo ordered his vanguard to ambush and butcher thirty unresisting Church emissaries carrying peace terms, burn their corpses in a lime pit, and plant forged republican pamphlets on the bodies to justify continuing the war. Andrés refused the order, broke his sword, and fled with the original parchment.</p>\n\n<h3>2. The Extraction Mission</h3>\n<p>The document is hidden in a lead scroll-case inside the hollowed altar-stone of Saint Severo. However, retrieving it presents multiple hazards:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Rodrigo's Inquisitors:</strong> Don Rodrigo has ordered four trusted hound-masters and ten elite dismounted caballeros to encircle the chapel the moment the bridge is breached, under strict orders to <em>'burn the chapel to the ground and let no one leave alive.'</em></li>\n  <li><strong>The Crypt Wards:</strong> The crypt is protected by ancient pre-Cataclysmic guardian traps: a swinging scythe pendulum (DC 14 Reflex / Dexterity check to avoid 2d8 damage) and a glyph of blinding flash (DC 13 Save vs. Spells).</li>\n  <li><strong>The Clock:</strong> Rodrigo intends to launch his assault at dawn. The PCs have four hours of darkness to slip into the village, retrieve the parchment, and decide Andrés's fate.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>3. How the PCs Can Use the Evidence</h3>\n<div class=\"hook-card info-card\">\n  <h4>Option 1: The Sovereign's Leash (Blackmail)</h4>\n  <p>The PCs confront Don Rodrigo in his private command tent with the sealed dispatch. Facing absolute public dishonor and trial under royal <a href=\"#rules/pundonor\" class=\"wiki-link\">Pundonor</a>, Rodrigo's arrogant defiance collapses. He agrees to recognize the PCs' absolute command over the royal garrisons, accept a permanent royal veto over troop movements, and spare the village.</p>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"hook-card info-card\">\n  <h4>Option 2: The Righteous Purge</h4>\n  <p>The PCs present the document before the assembled Grandees and the Restoration Council in Kordova, stripping Rodrigo of his rank and arresting him for high treason. However, this risks triggering a violent mutiny among his fiercely loyal heavy cavalry unless the PCs have secured their own independent troops.</p>\n</div>\n",
      "gmSecrets": "If Chancellor Marquis Mateo de Sadoria discovers the PCs possess this document, he will attempt to steal or buy it from them, seeking to use it to puppet Don Rodrigo himself.",
